.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.\" The text follows sync/main.js (usage line, exit codes), sync/protocol.js (verbs, flags) and the comments of the verbs in sync/engine.js.
.TH CETLI\-SYNC 1 "" "cetli"
.SH NAME
cetli\-sync \- the sync engine of cetli
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cetli\-sync
.I verb
.RI [ argument ...]
.PP
The verbs, with their arguments:
.PP
.B cetli\-sync status
.br
.B cetli\-sync setup
.br
.B cetli\-sync own\-id
.br
.B cetli\-sync host
.br
.B cetli\-sync join
.br
.B cetli\-sync finish
.br
.B cetli\-sync harden
.br
.B cetli\-sync reset
.br
.B cetli\-sync ensure
.br
.B cetli\-sync restart
.RB [ \-\-enable ]
.br
.B cetli\-sync forget
.I ID
.br
.B cetli\-sync forget \-\-all
.RB [ \-\-stop ]
.br
.B cetli\-sync revoke
.IR ID ...
.br
.B cetli\-sync promote
.IR ID ...
.br
.B cetli\-sync ack
.IR ID ...
.br
.B cetli\-sync ack \-\-all
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cetli\-sync
is the program behind the sync window of
.BR cetli (1).
It sets up and looks after a Syncthing instance of its own for the notes folder, and it connects the computers of one group (up to 10).
The window starts it for every step; it can also be started by hand in a terminal.
.PP
Each call does one verb and prints one JSON object per line on standard output.
The last line says how the call ended: it has the event
.B result
or the event
.BR error .
.PP
An
.I ID
is the device ID of a computer in the canonical form of Syncthing: 8 groups of 7 characters (A to Z and 2 to 7), joined by dashes.
IDs are positional arguments.
.SH VERBS
.TP
.B status
Reads the state of the sync set\-up and the computers of the group. It changes nothing.
.TP
.B setup
Sets up the instance (its own home directory and a configuration with the notes folder) and enables and starts the user unit
.BR cetli\-syncthing.service .
.TP
.B own\-id
Prints the ID of this computer.
.TP
.B host
Waits for one computer that wants to join, shows it, and accepts exactly the ID named on standard input
(one line:
.BI "accept " ID ).
It stops at once when standard input ends.
.TP
.B join
Reads the ID of the other computer from standard input (one line) and adds it. The ID is not an argument.
.TP
.B finish
Ends an open removal. It is meant to be run when the user has confirmed that.
.TP
.B harden
Takes the right to introduce other computers away from computers that only came in through another one.
It never deletes anything.
.TP
.B reset
Goes back to "not set up": stops and disables the unit and moves the instance directory aside under a time\-stamped name.
It deletes nothing. The notes are not touched; only the marker of the sync folder in the notes folder is taken away.
.TP
.B ensure
The quiet check that
.B cetli
makes once when it starts on a computer that is set up: it starts the sync program only when it is stopped and its unit is enabled,
and does nothing otherwise.
.TP
.BR restart " [" \-\-enable ]
Starts the user unit again when the sync program does not answer. It touches no data.
A unit that was switched off by the user is left off, unless
.B \-\-enable
is given.
.TP
.BI forget " ID"
Removes one computer that the user still has.
.TP
.BR "forget \-\-all" " [" \-\-stop ]
Removes all computers and shares. It never removes the folder or a file. With
.B \-\-stop
the unit is stopped and switched off as well.
.TP
.BI revoke " ID" ...
Removes a lost, stolen or unknown computer (the first ID) from the group, and with it the other IDs given, which the user marked as
"not mine".
.TP
.BI promote " ID" ...
Lets computers that were accepted directly introduce other computers.
.TP
.BI ack " ID" ...
.TP
.B ack \-\-all
Marks computers as seen. Only the state file of the engine changes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-all
With
.B forget
and
.BR ack :
all computers instead of the IDs.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
With
.BR "forget \-\-all" :
stop and switch off the unit as well.
.TP
.B \-\-enable
With
.BR restart :
switch on a unit that was switched off.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The call ended with a
.B result
line.
.TP
.B 1
The call ended with an
.B error
line.
.TP
.B 2
The command line is not one of the above. This line is printed on standard error:
.IP
.nf
usage: cetli\-sync status|setup|own\-id|host|join|finish|harden|reset | restart [\-\-enable] | ensure | forget <ID>|\-\-all [\-\-stop] | revoke|promote <ID>... | ack <ID>...|\-\-all
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I \(ti/.local/state/cetli/syncthing
The home directory of the Syncthing instance of cetli, with the state file of the engine
.RI ( cetli\-sync\-state.json ).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cetli/notes
The notes folder that is shared (\fI\(ti/.local/share/cetli/notes\fR if XDG_DATA_HOME is not set).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/cetli\-syncthing.service
The user unit that runs the instance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cetli (1)
